  "_heavy_longsword": "Longsword swing (without Better Combat): a horizontal cut, right to left, then the left-to-right return cut on the next swing (heavy_longsword_back; it uses heavy_longsword's duration). The blade turns round the grip like a clock hand while the hand moves a short way low across the view. rotation (on the entry) is the idle hold's blade heading and pivot the grip, both relative to vanilla's first-person hand: leave them unless the in-hand model changes. keys: at swing progress t (0..1), translation moves the hand from the idle hold (x right, y up, z toward the camera) and rotation is the blade's heading [pitch, yaw, roll] in degrees (yaw 0 = straight ahead, +90 = left; pitch raises the tip; roll twists the flat, 0 = flat facing up). Each key is eased in from the previous one (ease: linear, in, out, inout, in_cubic, out_cubic); the motion starts from and settles back to the idle hold. longsword_spin uses the same format (it plays with Better Combat too).",
